# fixtures/hex/store-a/seg.base.10.hex: store A's base segment ([F09 §16.1]), written by the rollup at
# lsn 19642: main's state at upto_lsn 16660 (rows #1-#16; #13-#15 absent), frozen bitsets, promoted fields,
# STATS, the view's schema, SYMTAB [1, ...), and every store-level table (runtime window up to 19475).
# Full-text tier 2 over every document of the view (the rollup builds it for the base, [F17 §6.4]): TERMS in
# front-coded blocks of 16, POST, DOCLEN for rows #1-#16 and FTSSTAT (candidate `kept` of HOLE(F09-doclen)).
# A base carries every FCOL and FIDX its FPROMO rows imply: no row holds assignee, so FCOL.assignee (0x4002) has
# every absent bit set and FIDX.assignee (0x5002) is its 16-byte header with n_values 0 ([F09 §10.1]-§10.3). The
# IDEM entries without result_inline hold result (0, 0), outside the heap order ([F11 §2.3], §8). Both as spec
# sync 2b (S2B-R-1, S2B-R-6) states them.

